{
  "sn22.22:0.1": "Linked Discourses 22.22 ",
  "sn22.22:0.2": "3. The Burden ",
  "sn22.22:0.3": "The Burden of Responsibility ",
  "sn22.22:1.1": "At Sāvatthī. ",
  "sn22.22:1.2": "“Mendicants, I will teach you the burden, the bearer of the burden, the taking up of the burden, and the putting down of the burden. ",
  "sn22.22:1.3": "Listen … ",
  "sn22.22:1.4": "And what is the burden? ",
  "sn22.22:1.5": "The five grasping aggregates, it should be said. ",
  "sn22.22:1.6": "What five? ",
  "sn22.22:1.7": "The grasping aggregates of form, feeling, perception, choices, and consciousness. ",
  "sn22.22:1.8": "This is called the burden. ",
  "sn22.22:2.1": "And who is the bearer of the burden? ",
  "sn22.22:2.2": "The individual, it should be said; ",
  "sn22.22:2.3": "the venerable of such name and such clan. ",
  "sn22.22:2.4": "This is called the bearer of the burden. ",
  "sn22.22:3.1": "And what is the taking up of the burden? ",
  "sn22.22:3.2": "It’s the craving that leads to future lives, mixed up with relishing and greed, taking pleasure there wherever it alights. That is, ",
  "sn22.22:3.3": "craving for sensual pleasures, craving for continued existence, and craving for nonexistence. ",
  "sn22.22:3.4": "This is called the taking up of the burden. ",
  "sn22.22:4.1": "And what is the putting down of the burden? ",
  "sn22.22:4.2": "It’s the fading away and cessation of that very same craving no residue left behind; giving it away, letting it go, releasing it, and not clinging to it. ",
  "s